authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.lem-tr-forced-greedy"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.lem-tr-forced-greedy"],"id":"long.lem-tr-forced-greedy","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Lemma 8.4 (Forced greedy)","locator":"Long record Lemma 8.4, p. 94, label lem:tr-forced-greedy","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For every $J\\ge2$: $w_n^{(J)}>T_{n+1}^{(J)}$ for all $n$ (the $q=1$ terms agree exactly, and every $q\\ge2$ tail term is strictly smaller than the corresponding weight term). Consequently the greedy support is the unique candidate support, and $\\mathrm{HalfRung}(J)$ holds iff the greedy orbit for $1/2$ under weights $w_n^{(J)}$ never lands in a fatal interval $(T_{n+1}^{(J)},w_n^{(J)})$. Rank $1$ is always a safe skip; ranks $2$ and $3$ are always takes.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.lem-tr-forced-greedy","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.lem-tr-forced-greedy","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.lem-tr-forced-greedy%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_forced_greedy_low_ranks%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.lem-tr-forced-greedy%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_forced_greedy_low_ranks%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_forced_greedy_low_ranks"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.lem-tr-forced-greedy","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e48